{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A terminal run with an open pull request is permanently excluded from lifecycle reconciliation, so a preexisting in-progress label can remain after merge and block later queue eligibility."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A posting identity change between a failed attempt and a retry whose response is lost causes recovery to miss the newly posted comment and publish a duplicate."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A valid priority re-approval within the same timestamp second as a failed run can be rejected until the owner approves again."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A run linked to enough inaccessible issues can exhaust every poll's request budget before later accessible issues receive lifecycle updates."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A label changed by a person between a failed transition and its retry can survive because recovery completes its saved plan using stale labels, leaving the issue blocked from the queue."}]}